 "issues": [
  "column split differs, totals agree for Q6: Vortex l_shipdate int16 + l_quantity int32, PIM l_shipdate int32 + l_quantity int16 (isr_spec.json operand_widths); both 14 vs 14.00 B/row; both sides call the split inferred from the 14.0 B/row pinned footprint",
  "Q1 input widths differ: Vortex 28 B/row (flags as cuDF strings 1 B + 4 B offset, as the real GPU) vs PIM 20.00 B/row (flags as 1-byte dictionary codes) -> favours PIM by 8 B/row; floors below are given at both widths",
  "owner's fused Q6 command reads 16.0 B/row (qty int32) vs 14.0 B/row for the general chain: the fused reference is not at the same widths",
  "Q6 filter parameters: both simulators use the dbgen default substitution (1994, 0.05-0.07, qty<24; Vortex SF1 result 114,160 selected rows); the real-GPU runs use 1997 / 0.02-0.04 / qty<24 on the Parquet data (114,271 rows, physical_floor.md). Same selectivity (1.90 %), different rows; the PIM main plan's cost does not depend on the selected count, the Vortex gathers do (114,160 items)",
  "clocks: simx core 2512 MHz, Ramulator2 AiM tCK 0.5 ns (2 GHz); both reported in us, no clock conversion is needed; the 5070's DRAM is GDDR7 and AiM is GDDR6 (projection)",
  "end of an operation: Vortex kernels end when DRAM has drained the writes (patched); results stay in DRAM except scalars/counts read back by the host (host step not simulated). PIM operators end with results in the bank rows (masks, write-backs) or in PU registers read by RD_MAC (sums, group accumulators); mask and compaction-segment read-out to the GPU are separate '+readout' variants",
  "mapping CSVs disagree on what the chain contains: Vortex mirrors the Sirius min/max SUM-widening pre-check (Q6 2 launches, Q1 10) while the PIM chains leave it out ('planner policy') -> chain row (a') drops it; Vortex omits Q1's batch_memcpy string path (6/batch) that PIM counts as 'removed'; Vortex mirrors the casts as launches that PIM folds into operand widths",
  "Q6 compaction is in the Vortex chain (count/scan/scatter + 2 gathers) but replaced by a mask in the PIM main chain: (a)/(d) mixes a plan change that a GPU could also make (masked aggregate)",
  "q6 SF0.01: speedup a/c S4 33.73 vs S1 12.50 differs > 10 %",
  "q6 SF0.01: speedup a/d S4 83.72 vs S1 31.03 differs > 10 %",
  "q6 SF0.01: speedup a/e S4 18.78 vs S1 6.96 differs > 10 %",
